certainly not easy to win, but White would retain good chances.}) 26... Bxe4
27. Rxe4 Rd1 28. e6 $2 Rxc1 29. e7+ Ke8 30. Nd5 f5 31. Re5 Rc2+ 32. Kf1 g3 {
Source: BCM, March 1963, p91} 0-1

